# Boot battery guard (#70 follow-up, owner report 2026-10-22): a cell
# resting under the floor must not start the firmware, drained latch or
# not. The sim boots at 3,350 mV with no charger and a clear latch
# (IPODUI_SIM_BATT_MV, IPODUI_SIM_DRAINED=0;
# uisimulator/common/powermgmt-sim.c), under BB_FLOOR_MV (3,400, the
# same on the target): apps/main.c's bootbatt_enforce(), right after
# lcd_init(), draws the glyph-only low-battery image
# (ui_sys_dead_battery(), captured as dead-battery.png; no boot logo
# first, so no boot-fw.png), holds it 2 s and powers off before storage,
# fonts, the latch or any write. The sim exits there, so nothing below
# runs: no settings, no database, no shell.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p16-bootbatt-refuse.script
# env: IPODUI_SIM_BATT_MV=3350
# env: IPODUI_SIM_DRAINED=0
# illusion: preboot the guard powers off right after lcd_init(), before the shell and its text watch
# boot_shot
# golden: skip
# log: bootbatt refuse mv=3350 thr=3400
# log: sys deadbatt drawn=1
# log: bootbatt off writes=0
# nolog: bootbatt boot
# nolog: bootbatt plugged
# nolog: bootbatt latch
# nolog: boot screen gen=
# nolog: splash-pass

wait 3000
shot never_reached       # the sim powered off in init(): no such shot
